Q: Salesforce Opportunity StageName: set default value and make it read-only for users but editable via API/Apex A: <blockquote>
<p>set the default Stage (especially if record types exist)</p>
</blockquote>
<p><code>before insert</code> trigger plus the Spring'26 feature (you may have a preview org already; if not - wait 1-2 weeks) <a href="https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=release-notes.rn_apex_extract_picklist_values.htm&amp;release=260&amp;type=5" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=release-notes.rn_apex_extract_picklist_values.htm&amp;release=260&amp;type=5</a></p>
<pre><code>ConnectApi.PicklistValuesCollection picklistCollection = 
    ConnectApi.RecordUi.getPicklistValuesByRecordType('Opportunity', recordTypeId);

// Access any picklist field's values
ConnectApi.PicklistValues statusValues = 
    picklistCollection.picklistFieldValues.get('StageName');
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>they should not be able to change it in UI</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's an enum called Quiddity (&quot;essence of being; what are you exactly&quot;) for determining whether the action is from UI / batch job / data load... You can shoot yourself in the foot very badly, most of the time we do not want the system to &quot;behave 1 way when accessed in UI, another way when doing bulk load&quot;)... Something like this?</p>
<p>Values: <a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.apexref.meta/apexref/apex_enum_System_Quiddity.htm" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.apexref.meta/apexref/apex_enum_System_Quiddity.htm</a></p>
<pre><code>Request reqInfo = Request.getCurrent();
Quiddity currentType = reqInfo.getQuiddity();
if(currentType != Quiddity.BATCH_APEX &amp;&amp; opp.StageName != oldOpp.StageName){
    opp.StageName.addError('Don\'t');
}
</code></pre>
